    "circularity_finding": "YES \u2014 CO2 Mass (short tons) and Heat Input (mmBtu) in EPA CAMPD exhibit a strongly circular relationship across both Coal (Pearson r >= 0.9998) and Natural Gas / Pipeline Natural Gas (Pearson r >= 0.99998), with over 90% of operating hours following a constant per-unit stoichiometric factor (CO2 Mass / Heat Input) to within +/-0.0002 short tons/mmBtu. Under 40 CFR Part 75 Appendix G (fuel-based CO2 calculation for gas units via Fc = 1,040 scf CO2/mmBtu) and Appendix F (stack flow + diluent Fc equations where both CO2 mass and heat input are derived from the same stack flow and diluent analyzers), CO2 Mass and Heat Input are mathematically co-derived even when the CAMPD Measure Indicator is labelled 'Measured' (which indicates non-substituted primary monitoring rather than independent CO2 vs. heat-input instruments). Therefore, comparing reported CO2 Mass against reported Heat Input detects naive single-channel tampering, but cannot by itself stop a coordinated insider who scales both channels together unless paired with Gross Load (MW) co-movement and an independent fuel custody-transfer meter (synthetic_fuel_flow_mmbtu_indep / fuel_ledger_synthetic)."
  }
